Good Afternoon Students,

We are excited to announce an Industrial Visit to the Akshaya Patra Foundation, Kandi, Hyderabad, scheduled for 23rd August 2025.

The Akshaya Patra Foundation is a non-profit organization dedicated to eliminating classroom hunger and malnutrition.
In collaboration with the Government of India and state governments, Akshaya Patra implements the PM POSHAN Abhiyaan 
(formerly the Mid-Day Meal Scheme) through a Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model.
Their efforts support the Right to Food and Right to Education for children from challenging socio-economic backgrounds.

Since 2000, Akshaya Patra has grown from serving 1,500 children in Bengaluru to providing mid-day meals to 2 million children across 15 states and
2 union territories, with the support of government bodies, corporate partners, donors, and volunteers. 
The Foundation ensures hygienically prepared, nutritious meals to empower children to learn, grow, and achieve their potential.

Vision: No child in India shall be deprived of education due to hunger
Mission: To feed 3 million children by 2025

